## WHAT THE DRAFTER FOUND (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER at main `8858e5d1`; the tree read as the tarball of that commit, 1059 files, extracted to scratch; contrast by the repo's own `contrastRatio` through jest and by a stand-alone sRGB program, both agreeing to two places)
1. **The three greys and their real grounds.** `.metric-card .metric-label` `#7f8c8d` (`index-styles.css:112`) on the card ground `white` (`.metric-card`, line 86): 3.48. `.file-description` (`:567`) on `.import-section` `#f8f9fa`: 3.30. `.drop-text` (`:592`) on `.file-drop-zone` `white` (`:578`): 3.48. The brand chrome text colour `#00719f` is 5.44 on white and 5.16 on `#f8f9fa`.
2. **THE TRAP: dark mode, and two guards that read dark-mode.css.** `.metric-label` and `.file-description` already have dark rules (`dark-mode.css:127`, `:1218`, both `#8c8c8c`, which beat the light rules by specificity), so changing their light colour moves no dark pixel. **`.drop-text` has NO dark rule**: today it shows `#7f8c8d` on the dark panel ground `#1c1c1c` at 4.90 (passes). Moving only its light colour to `#00719f` would put 3.13 on dark, a NEW failure. My first draft added `body.dark-mode .drop-text { color: #7f8c8d; }` to keep the dark pixels, and it was MEASURED RED in the run list: `brand-shell-tokens.test.js` ("a light-only value must never become a legal dark-mode.css value": it names `#7f8c8d`) and `brand-token-conformance.test.js` ("every hex in dark-mode.css resolves to a token ... The manifest is CLOSED to new entries": `#7f8c8d`, 1x). **So the lane joins `.drop-text` to the existing dark muted-text list** (`body.dark-mode .file-description,` gains a line `body.dark-mode .drop-text,`), colour `#8c8c8c`, a recorded token: dark moves from 4.90 to 5.07, a tiny improvement and the only dark pixel change of the lane. Cells D3 and D4 hold it.
3. **Why a search for `.drop-text` never found it in the static sweep (the ticket's "unexplained asymmetry").** MEASURED in jest: after the change the light failure set of `static/index.html` loses `p.file-description x3` AND `span x3` (the sweep reports a node by tag and own classes; the three import-modal drop texts are `<span>` children of `div.drop-text`, so they were listed as a bare `span x3`, not under `.drop-text`). The ticket's belief that `.drop-text` is "not in the baseline" was a search for the class name; it was in the baseline as `span x3`. The signature leaving with exactly this change is the evidence; the three spans are not individually named by the program (inferred, not run-proved by node identity).
4. **RD-175: no single text colour can work, so the label gets its own ground.** The label is centred over the whole 20px track, across the fill and the unfilled track. White on the four fills: black `#2c3e50` 10.98 (passes), cyan `#00bcd4` 2.30, magenta `#e91e63` 4.35, yellow `#ffc107` 1.63; white on the track 1.19; dark ink `#212529` on the black fill start 1.40. Either colour fails somewhere, and the fill width varies from 0 to 100 percent. So the label becomes a small OPAQUE chip (`#212529` on `#ffffff`, 15.43; padding `0 6px`, radius 8px, `line-height: 1.25` so it is 16px tall in a 20px bar) and the text-shadow (the mitigation) is removed, with the reason in the rule's comment. Dark: the chip is `#dedede` on `#1c1c1c` (12.67) and the track `#e9ecef` becomes `#313131` (the project's own dark border value), which is the ticket's own dark recommendation. **The light chip ground is written `white`, not `#ffffff`**: `brand-token-conformance.test.js` pins the occurrence count of the surface-card token `#ffffff` in the light sheets (`scripts/derive-brand-tokens.js:148`, 51) and my first draft's `background: #ffffff` made it 52 (MEASURED RED: "pins x51, measured x52"); changing that pin means regenerating `static/css/tokens.css`, which this lane does not own. The keyword `white` is already how the card grounds are written (`.metric-card`, `.file-drop-zone`) and is measured by the same helper. The RD-85 geometry (sibling, centred, no clip, nowrap, `pointer-events: none`) is kept (cell C3).
